 ## Gem Sniping
 
 ### ADB input (v25, live BlueStacks validation pending)
+
+**ADB focus compatibility fix:** reads the complete Android WindowManager dump
+instead of the window-list-only view, which can omit current focus on Android
+11. When the focus field is absent, it checks ActivityTaskManager's top-resumed
+activity. Null, unreadable or conflicting focus still stops input; permission
+dialogs are not accepted as the game. If the connection preview still cannot
+identify the app, confirm that the configured ADB port belongs to the exact
+BlueStacks instance running the game. No desktop-mouse fallback is used.
 
 **Sniping settings → Input method → ADB** sends screenshots, taps and swipes through the selected Android device. It does not move the PC cursor, send Windows keys or bring BlueStacks to the foreground. Mouse mode remains the default for existing settings. Only Gem Sniping uses ADB; the Map overlay and ordinary Gem Watch continue using the visible Windows desktop.
 
